# Two advisories currently have no fix, so `npm audit` fails at its default level:
#   - GHSA-gcqx-w48m-w2h4 (low): deepmerge <= 4.3.1 has no patched release (4.3.1 is
#     the latest). Dev-only, reached through jest-config (jest).
#   - GHSA-g3hv-75wg-m249 (moderate): the minimatch copy bundled inside aws-cdk-lib
#     2.275.0, which npm overrides cannot reach. Needs a new aws-cdk-lib release.
# The gate is therefore raised to "high" so that low and moderate findings no longer
# fail the audit, while high and critical ones still do.
# Remove the audit-level line (back to the default) once both are fixed upstream.
audit-level=high
